Strategy 1: Sequential (Sorted) File with Sparse Primary Index on TxnID 

Principle: Records are physically ordered on disk by TxnID (which arrives in increasing order). A sparse primary index maintains one <TxnID, BlockPtr> entry per data block.  

Justification: Because TxnID is monotonically increasing, new records append cleanly to the end of the file without shifting existing blocks, while range queries (hourly reconciliation of 2,000 records) read contiguous blocks sequentially.  

